    question_en: "A mobile game studio, AetherForge Studios, operates a popular multiplayer mobile game with millions of active players distributed globally. The mobile application allows players to upload gameplay replay recordings and crash diagnostic archives, ranging from 300 MB to 1.5 GB in size, directly to a centralized Amazon S3 bucket located in the us-east-1 Region.\n\nMany players report that uploads frequently fail or take an excessively long time due to long geographic distances and intermittent mobile connectivity. In addition, an internal financial review reveals that storage costs for the S3 bucket are steadily increasing due to abandoned, uncompleted upload parts remaining in the bucket indefinitely.\n\nA solutions architect must implement a solution that maximizes upload speeds for players worldwide, increases upload reliability over unstable mobile networks, and automatically eliminates storage costs from failed upload attempts with the least operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
