    question_en: "A mobile game studio hosts dedicated multiplayer game servers on Amazon EC2 instances managed by an Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. The instances launch from an Amazon Machine Image (AMI) backed by an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) snapshot containing game engine binaries and pre-rendered 3D assets.\n\nDuring live tournament events, sudden traffic surges cause the Auto Scaling group to rapidly scale out. However, players assigned to newly launched instances experience severe frame stuttering and high disk read latency during the first 10 to 15 minutes of gameplay. Performance stabilizes and runs smoothly for all subsequent matches on those same instances. A solutions architect must eliminate this initial storage latency for newly launched servers with the least operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution will meet these requirements?",
