    question_en: "SkyVista Airlines, a regional carrier, is migrating its online flight booking and reservation platform to AWS. The architecture must achieve high availability across two Availability Zones (AZs) and fulfill the following requirements:\n- Public-facing Application Load Balancers (ALBs) must receive booking requests from passengers over the internet.\n- An application tier consisting of Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group must have outbound internet connectivity to communicate with third-party payment gateways and airline Global Distribution System (GDS) APIs, but must not be directly accessible from the internet.\n- A database tier running an Amazon RDS Multi-AZ DB cluster to store Passenger Name Records (PNR) and ticketing data must be strictly isolated with no inbound or outbound internet access.\n\nWhich subnet design and routing configuration should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?",
