    question_en: "A regional airline operates a ticket booking web application on AWS. The application tier runs on Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer, and the data tier uses a Multi-AZ Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. During seasonal promotional flight sales, tens of thousands of users submit identical search queries for popular flight schedules and seat availability. Database monitoring indicates that the RDS instance CPU utilization consistently exceeds 90% due to repeated SELECT queries, causing search latency to spike from under 100 milliseconds to several seconds.\n\nA solutions architect must resolve this performance bottleneck by reducing read latency to sub-milliseconds and offloading repeated queries from the database. The caching layer must also support high availability with automatic failover.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
