    question_en: "A healthcare records startup stores anonymized electronic health record (EHR) audit logs as daily JSON files in an Amazon S3 bucket. Data analysts occasionally need to run ad-hoc SQL queries on this data to generate compliance and usage reports. The record schema frequently evolves as new medical telemetry and tracking fields are introduced. The startup requires a solution that automatically detects schema changes, minimizes query execution costs, and eliminates the operational overhead of managing server infrastructure.\n\nWhich combination of actions should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)",
