    question_en: "A healthcare startup runs an electronic health record (EHR) ingestion service on Amazon EC2 instances. During peak hours, processing large medical document batches occasionally causes memory leaks, resulting in application hangs. A solutions architect must implement a solution to monitor operating system-level memory utilization, automatically restart the ingestion daemon when memory utilization exceeds 85%, and send an alert notification to the operations team.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
