    question_en: "A healthcare records startup runs a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances in private subnets across multiple Availability Zones within a VPC. The application running on these instances processes confidential patient diagnostic images and electronic health records that are stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. Due to strict healthcare compliance standards, patient data must not traverse the public internet. Additionally, the company wants to eliminate data transfer charges incurred by NAT Gateways and ensure secure, seamless authentication from the instances to Amazon S3 without storing long-term credentials on the servers.\n\nWhich combination of actions should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)",
