    question_en: "A healthcare technology startup hosts its HIPAA-compliant electronic health records (EHR) web application in the us-east-1 Region. The primary architecture consists of an Application Load Balancer (ALB), an Auto Scaling group of Amazon EC2 instances, and an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL Multi-AZ database instance.\n\nThe company wants to establish a disaster recovery (DR) solution in the us-west-2 Region to protect against regional outages. The company has defined the following requirements:\n- Recovery Point Objective (RPO) of no more than 15 minutes.\n- Recovery Time Objective (RTO) of no more than 45 minutes.\n- Minimize ongoing infrastructure costs and avoid paying for running compute instances in the secondary Region during normal operations.\n\nWhich architecture should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
