    question_en: "A digital healthcare startup is developing a new portal for partner clinics to securely upload electronic health records (EHR) and patient intake PDFs. The development team has limited cloud operations staff and wants to minimize operational overhead.\n\nThe web front-end and API layer must be deployed quickly with automatic scaling, load balancing, and health monitoring without managing the underlying infrastructure configuration directly. When clinics upload documents, each file is stored in an Amazon S3 bucket and requires an immediate, lightweight parsing task (taking less than 20 seconds per document) to extract patient metadata and sanitize Protected Health Information (PHI).\n\nWhich combination of actions should the solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)",
