    question_en: "A healthcare startup is modernizing its electronic health records (EHR) platform. The startup has the following requirements:\n\n- External clinical laboratories and partner diagnostic centers must continue uploading batch lab results and patient records using their existing Secure File Transfer Protocol (SFTP) workflows without modifying client applications.\n- On-premises clinic staff need fast, low-latency access over the local network using the Server Message Block (SMB) protocol to browse and edit recently generated medical reports.\n- All patient records must be consolidated and stored centrally in Amazon S3 for high durability, automated lifecycle tiering, and downstream analytics.\n- The solution must minimize operational overhead.\n\nWhich combination of actions will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
